    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1400">

                <pb facs="1747" n="1547" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1547"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 (Potsdam)/8–145</note>
                <head>No. 1400<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the French
                        Minister of Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Bidault</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/> No. 678</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-01">August 1, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have just received a communication
                    from Potsdam by telephone<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1400-f1"/> from the Secretary of
                    State instructing me to communicate to the Government of France a statement
                    which has been adopted by the Three Powers at the Conference concerning the
                    trial of war criminals.</p>
                <p>You will note that the three Governments will be most grateful if the French
                    Government will treat the present communication as strictly secret until such
                    time as an official statement is issued by the Conference.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Caffery</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d1400-a1.xml" xpointer="d1400-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1400-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1400-f1-content">
                <p>A copy of the instruction to the British Ambassador at Paris to make a similar
                    approach to the French Government bears the following manuscript notation:
                    “Telephoned Caffery Aug 1, 6:00 p.m.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
